==Part 2: Empress' Call to Arms==
There is only one map in this part: [[The Gates of Aku|Unleashing the Cats]], which appears after clearing all Part 1 stages listed above. It has no time limit and contains only one stage, which disappears when cleared, so it can only be beaten once per save file. By completing this map, you will receive 100 Cat Food via missions and unlock several new features, including the first map of Part 3:

*[[The Aku Realms]]: A new area in [[Empire of Cats]] containing a wide range of enemies. Every Aku Realm stage you complete reduces the level handicap imposed by the [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]] by 1. Clear all Aku Realm stages to receive one-time rewards of 1 Gold [[Catfruit]] and 1 [[Platinum Capsules (Gacha Event)|Platinum Ticket]].
**[[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|Mount Aku Invasion]]: A bonus stage that appears in [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku/Mount Fuji]] after clearing all other Aku Realms. Clear to unlock [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] and strip the Aku Altar of its ability to disable + levels.
*[[Aku's Melody (Merciless)|Temptation's Symphony]]: An [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] from which you can unlock [[Pied Piper Cat (Rare Cat)|Pied Piper Cat]], who is able to break [[Shield]]s and weaken Aku enemies. Appears on the 9th, 10th, 23rd, and 24th of every month.
*[[Imminent Disaster]]: The 39th sub-chapter of [[Uncanny Legends]]. Requires [[Spacetime Distortion]] to be cleared before it can be challenged.
*[[Empress' Report 1]] and [[Empress' Excavation 1]]: See below.

==Part 3A: Empress' Report==
This part sees a return to the four-stage maps that appear for two hours a day. There are a total of five maps this time, one unlocked after the other, and they have several rewards including [[Gamatoto Expedition|Catamins]], Legend [[Catseye]]s, [[Battle Items]] and Aku [[Catfruit]] Seeds. Each reward can only be claimed once; completing all maps in this part awards 3 [[Platinum Capsules (Gacha Event)|Platinum Shards]] via missions.

Empress' Reports [[Empress' Report 3|3]], [[Empress' Report 4|4]] and [[Empress' Report 5|5]] introduce more new Aku, including [[Miz Devil]], [[Medu-san]] and [[Deathkory]], respectively.

